XLibre live property fixture (2026-10-25)
==========================================

- Add an opt-in installed consumer that mutates a writable XLibre output
  `DPI` property, waits for the coalesced shell observer transaction, verifies
  shell/descendant scale and callback output identity, and restores the
  original property on every exit path. Without a supplied XLibre display it
  explicitly returns the ordinary-Xvfb skip status; no fallback run is counted
  as live qualification.
- Add a source-contract regression for the live fixture's property restoration,
  teardown ordering, callback cardinality and real-display/status-77 boundary.
- Record live-fixture source and installed-`libXm` fingerprints, exact compile/
  run commands, elapsed time and the qualification result in `receipt.json`.
- Classify the receipt result explicitly as `pass`, `skip` or `fail`, keeping a
  successful ordinary-Xvfb rejection distinct from real-display qualification.

