  distinct from future real-XLibre qualification.

Display-scale transaction reentrancy guard (2026-10-25)
=========================================================

- Reject nested `XmSetDisplayScaleOverride`/display-scale transactions from
  a scale callback, preserving the outer override as authoritative. The
  installed fixture verifies callback invocation, nested rejection and
  cleanup; per-display transaction state is retired with the Motif display.

XLibre transient-query fallback (2026-10-25)
==============================================

- Return to the global display scale when a realized shell's client-area or
  RandR resource query is temporarily unavailable, instead of retaining a
  stale per-output scale. The source-contract regression covers initialization
  and each early-return fallback; real output hotplug qualification remains a
  separate XLibre gate.

XLibre vendor predicate hardening (2026-10-25)
================================================

- Require the server vendor string to be exactly `XLibre` or `XLibre` followed
  by whitespace and a version suffix. Substrings such as `NotXLibre` and
  `XLibre-server` are no longer treated as the versioned XLibre contract; the
  installed fixture covers positive, spoofed and malformed vendor names.

XLibre RandR property decode hardening (2026-10-25)
====================================================

- Validate the RandR property type, format, item count and trailing-byte
  metadata before reading the returned format-32 buffer. Malformed format-8
  or format-16 properties are now rejected without an out-of-bounds read;
  the installed contract fixture exercises the decode boundary under the
  sanitizer configuration.

