	* Add additive XmAvatar presentation with borrowed-pixmap validation,
	  deterministic initials fallback, explicit sizing and accessibility;
	  see docs/avatar.md.

2026-10-26
    XmScale now draws non-Xft value labels through its Motif render table
    when available, preserving compound-string and locale text handling;
    the direct XDrawImageString path remains only as a no-table fallback.

SegmentedControl relayout redraw (2026-10-27)
===============================================

- Resource changes for RTL order, spacing, or clear-selection behavior now
  request redisplay after relayout instead of returning a false SetValues
  result.

Compound-string label ownership (2026-10-27)
=============================================

- StatusBar, Toolbar, Toast, and Skeleton now copy `XmString` labels directly
  instead of flattening them through a locale byte string, preserving charset
  segments and multilingual text. StatusBar progress suffixes and Toolbar
  shortcuts are concatenated as `XmString` segments for the same reason.

Toast SetValues redraw (2026-10-27)
===================================

- Toast now reports changed message, action, and timeout resources from
  `SetValues`; action visibility uses `XmStringEmpty` without flattening text.

CommandPalette compound-string ownership (2026-10-27)
=======================================================

- CommandPalette now copies item labels and shortcuts as `XmString` values,
  preserving compound-string charset segments in its stored item model.

Divider and Chip compound-string ownership (2026-10-27)
========================================================

- Divider and Chip now retain caller labels with `XmStringCopy` instead of
  flattening charset segments through a locale byte string.

Avatar, Badge, and DropHighlight compound-string ownership (2026-10-27)
=========================================================================

- Avatar initials, Badge labels, and DropHighlight labels now retain
  compound-string charset segments with direct `XmString` copies.

